.TH "OPS" 1 "" "ops" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ops \- run the fleet
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBops\fR [flags] <command>
.PP
A word starting with \fB@\fR names a response file (\fB@args\fR), whose lines
are read as arguments, one per line, until \fB\-\-\fR; to pass a word starting
with \fB@\fR, double it (\fB@@x\fR).
.SH "COMMANDS"
.TP
\fBnote\fR
add a note
.TP
\fBexec\fR
run a command
.TP
\fBrun\fR
run a command on a host
.SH "DATA"
Commands that read a document from standard input.
.TP
\fBimport\fR
import tasks
.TP
\fBupper\fR
upper\-case lines (experimental)
.SH "DEPLOYING"
Commands that change what runs where.
Each one asks before it acts.
.TP
\fBdeploy\fR
ship a service (beta)
.SH "HELP TOPICS"
.TP
\fBfilters\fR
how filters work
.TP
\fBenvironment\fR
the environment variables ops reads
.SH "OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
print help
.SH "OUTPUT"
Flags that shape what ops prints.
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
say more (repeatable)
.br
repeat to count: \-vvv
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fIstring\fR
when to color (default auto) [auto|always|never]
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\fBOPS_TOKEN\fR \fIstring\fR
the API token (length >= 20)
.sp
Get one from the console.
.sp
\&.Keep it secret; a path such as C:\eops\etoken works too.
.br
at least 20 characters
.TP
\fBOPS_LOG\fR \fIstring\fR
the log level [debug|info|error]
.RS
.RS 2
\fBdebug\fR \- everything
.br
\fBinfo\fR
.br
\fBerror\fR \- failures only
.RE
.RE
.SH CONFIGURATION
.TP
\fBregion\fR (region) \fIstring\fR
the default region (beta)
.sp
The region commands use when none is given.
.br
must look like eu\-1
.TP
\fBprofile\fR (profile) \fIstring\fR
the output profile [short|long]
.RS
.RS 2
\fBshort\fR \- one line each
.br
\fBlong\fR \- every field
.RE
.RE
.SH "SEE ALSO"
\fBops\-deploy\fR(1), \fBops\-import\fR(1), \fBops\-upper\fR(1),
\fBops\-note\fR(1), \fBops\-exec\fR(1), \fBops\-run\fR(1),
\fBops\-filters\fR(1), \fBops\-environment\fR(1)
